# nextscrum-specs-kit default .gitignore
#
# A broad, multi-stack default: keep secrets, personal and editor files, OS junk,
# and build artifacts out of git regardless of stack. RESKIN: delete the sections
# that do not apply to this project, and add anything stack-specific.
#
# Note: .gitignore only stops untracked FILES from being committed. It cannot
# scrub a secret pasted INTO a tracked file. The security baseline in
# .claude/rules/engineering.md ("no secrets in source") and code review cover that.

# --- Secrets and credentials (never commit) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
service-account*.json
gha-creds-*.json
.npmrc
.netrc
secrets.*
*.secret
# Public certificates are sometimes committed on purpose; remove the next line if so.
*.crt

# --- Local / personal tool settings ---
.claude/settings.local.json
docs/agent-telemetry.jsonl
scripts/.self-test-telemetry.jsonl

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Editors / IDEs ---
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.classpath
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace

# --- Logs and temp ---
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
.cache/
*.tmp
*.pid

# --- Dependencies ---
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
jspm_packages/
bower_components/
.yarn/cache
.yarn/unplugged
.bundle/
# Composer (PHP) and some Go projects commit vendor/; remove the next line if yours does.
vendor/

# --- Build / compiled output ---
dist/
build/
out/
.output/
.next/
.nuxt/
.svelte-kit/
.turbo/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
target/
obj/
*.class
*.o
*.obj
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Local artifacts ---
*.local
_shot-*.png
*.bak
*.orig
